+# Window-rule attribution — round-24 stale-source control
+
+This control reuses only the previously opened S016–S020 rows. The quotes below are exact substrings of their cited source bytes; they are not new source openings or observations.
+
+| Claim | Statement | Source | Quote |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| A1 | Current docs' `getprop` heading names a property reader but does not establish rule attribution on this host. | S016 | "getprop" |
+| A2 | The wiki's `match` field documents the condition used to select windows for a rule. | S017 | "match" |
+| A3 | The wiki describes `props` as matching inputs rather than effects applied after selection. | S017 | "props" |
+| A4 | The tagged handler reads `PROP` after selecting a window, so a returned value remains effect data. | S018 | "PROP" |
+| A5 | The tagged source registers `getprop` as a command; it does not return a matching rule identity. | S018 | "getprop" |
+| A6 | The captured `getprop` usage takes both a regex and a property argument. | S019 | "hyprctl [flags] getprop <regex> <property>" |
+| A7 | The default `windowrule` applies opacity after tagging all windows for default opacity. | S020 | "windowrule = opacity 0.97 0.9, match:tag default-opacity" |
+| A8 | The terminal `windowrule` removes its default-opacity tag before applying terminal opacity. | S020 | "windowrule = opacity 0.97 0.9, match:tag terminal" |
